│ To access your Windows files using wintux bash shell:      │                                                                    │
│ mnt-win              # prompts for Windows credentials     │
│ mnt-win  user  pass  # non-interactive, automounts WinTux  │
│ mnt-win --save       # Save creds to auto-mount on reboot  │
│ mnt-win --umount     # unmounts /mnt/win from Windows      │
╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
│ WinTux FS is Amnesiac - files in / disappears on vm reboot │
│ Only writes made to Windows at: /mnt/win stay persistent!  │
╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮ 
│ First time only, on the Windows side (as admin)  >  ╰─CMD.exe─╮
│ C:\> net share WinTux="%USERPROFILE%" /GRANT:%USERNAME%,FULL  │ 
